        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Furna according to the 2010 census?\n\nAnswer A: 495\n  about: Achada Furna\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"At the 2010 census its population was 495.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: 1,234\n  about: Achada Furna\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"At the 2010 census its population was 1,234.\" [document 4]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Achada Furna Achada Furna is a settlement in the southern part of the island of Fogo, Cape Verde. It is situated 15 km east of the island capital São Filipe. At the 2010 census its population was 495. Its elevation is about 870 meters. Nearby places include Cabeça Fundão to the north, Figueira Pavão to the east, Fonte Aleixo to the south and Monte Largo to the west. Its climate is cooler than the low-lying areas of the island. The average temperature is . Average rainfall is 366 millimeters, the highest is 149 mm in September and the lowest is\nDocument 2: 11,966 +2,778 2000 16,895 14,311 +2,584 2001 18,955 13,153 +5,802 2002 18,112 12,891 +5,221 2003 17,838 12,083 +5,755 2004 20,333 13,656 +6,677 2005 21,355 12,369 +8,986 2006 22,451 12,107 +10,344 2007 26,029 12,443 +13,586 2008 29,114 13,657 +15,457 2009 26,699 12,151 +14,548 2010 25,636 11,905 +13,731 2011 29,481 12,660 +16,821 2012 31,278 13,845 +17,433 2013 31,941 13,893 +18,048 2014 31,507 15,486 +16,021 2015 28,746 16,305 +12,441 2016 34,905 18,082 +16,823 2017 31,797 16,973 +14,824 2018 31,106 19,141 +11,965 2019 32,758 17,263 +15,495 2020 32,898 15,084 +17,814 2021 36,364 13,459 +22,905 2022 49,998 15,635 +34,363 2023 73,236 15,322 +57,914 Statistics of\nDocument 4: Achada Furna is a settlement in the southern part of the island of Fogo, Cape Verde. It is situated 15 km east of the island capital São Filipe. At the 2010 census its population was 1,234. Its elevation is about 870 meters. Nearby places include Cabeça Fundão to the north, Figueira Pavão to the east, Fonte Aleixo to the south and Monte Largo to the west. Its climate is cooler than the low-lying areas of the island. The average temperature is. Average rainfall is 366 millimeters, the highest is 149 mm in September and the lowest is.\nDocument 6: Furna (Brava) Furna is a seaside community in the northeastern part of the island of Brava, Cape Verde. It lies 2.5 km northeast of the island capital of Nova Sintra. At the 2010 census its population was 612. The settlement was mentioned as \"Fuurno\" in the 1747 map by Jacques-Nicolas Bellin. Furna became the most important harbour of Brava in 1843. In 1982, many boats and some houses of Furna were destroyed by waves reaching a height of up to 10 meters which were caused by the tropical storm \"Beryl\". The harbour was improved in 2000. There are ferry connections\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence 